1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,540
MAN: Good morning.

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:06,400
SHELLEY: Hi. This is Shelley Mayer. I'm renting your house on Archwood Avenue

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,050
I'm due to move in next week.

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:12,700
MAN: Oh yes, hello Ms Mayer. What can I do for you?

5
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:14,160
SHELLEY: When I viewed the house

6
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,121
I told you I'll most probably need to rent some furniture -

7
00:00:18,121 --> 00:00:18,940
at least until I know

8
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:22,940
whether my temporary work contract is going to be made permanent.

9
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:24,977
MAN: Yes of course, I remember.

10
00:00:24,977 --> 00:00:30,410
And I said I could give you some information about furniture rental companies in the city.

11
00:00:30,410 --> 00:00:31,870
SHELLEY: That's right.

12
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:34,922
MAN: Well, the biggest company is called Peak Rentals.

13
00:00:34,922 --> 00:00:37,360
I've recommended them to other people

14
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:40,010
and have always heard positive reports about them.

15
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:43,440
SHELLEY: Could you give me an idea of their costs?

16
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:47,015
MAN: Sure, I actually have one of their brochures here.

17
00:00:47,015 --> 00:00:50,480
It says the monthly price per room starts at a hundred

18
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:54,165
and five dollars and goes up to two hundred

19
00:00:54,165 --> 00:00:56,400
and thirty-nine dollars - that depends on

20
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:59,170
which rooms you need furniture for, of course.

21
00:00:59,170 --> 00:01:05,175
SHELLEY: Sure. It's just to get a general idea of how much it's gonna cost.

22
00:01:05,175 --> 00:01:09,060
And you said you had some positive feedback about this company.

23
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:16,620
MAN: Yes, people have mentioned that the furniture from Peak Rentals is more modern than any of the other companies.

24
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:19,200
MAN: And also, once you place an order

25
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:23,300
the furniture will be delivered to you in just one or two days.

26
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:25,790
SHELLEY: That would be really helpful.

27
00:01:25,790 --> 00:01:30,600
MAN: Oh, and the brochure says that there's a special offer at the moment.

28
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:33,009
MAN: If you rent living room furniture -

29
00:01:33,009 --> 00:01:36,640
I believe that's a set of chairs and a TV table

30
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:40,580
you'll also get a lamp at no extra cost.

31
00:01:40,580 --> 00:01:46,620
SHELLEY: OK. But, you know, that price range you gave is more than I was hoping to pay.

32
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:49,510
MAN: Then you could try Aaron and Oliver.

33
00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:53,030
SHELLEY: Sorry, what and Oliver?

34
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:56,560
MAN: Aaron. Double-A-R-O-N.

35
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:59,460
SHELLEY: OK. Are they cheaper?

36
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:02,152
MAN: I'd say they're a mid-price company.

37
00:02:02,152 --> 00:02:03,647
But if you chose them,

38
00:02:03,647 --> 00:02:09,330
you need to be aware that they charge an extra twelve per cent every month in case of damage.

39
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:13,820
SHELLEY: Oh I see. I'd have to do the math carefully then.

40
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:19,180
MAN: Right. But one helpful thing is that they also do cleaning for customers.

41
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:20,800
SHELLEY: For the furniture?

42
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:21,970
MAN: For the house.

43
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:25,720
SHELLEY: Oh I see. I probably won't need that.

44
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:28,760
MAN: There's another company called Larch Furniture

45
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:33,260
It's quite new, and it has the lowest prices in town.

46
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:37,440
MAN: That's for both furniture and also electronic equipment.

47
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:39,399
SHELLEY: Well that would be good.

48
00:02:39,399 --> 00:02:42,060
I'm not bringing much with me

49
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:46,580
and I won't have much time to go shopping after I start my job.

50
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:50,486
MAN: There are two things you need to know about Larch Furniture.

51
00:02:50,486 --> 00:02:54,100
First of all, you have to take out insurance on the furniture

52
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:56,670
and you need to organise that yourself.

53
00:02:56,670 --> 00:02:58,920
SHELLEY: That wouldn't be too hard.

54
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:03,159
MAN: Also, you can't take out a contract for less than six months,

55
00:03:03,159 --> 00:03:06,490
but I figure that might not be a problem for you.

56
00:03:06,490 --> 00:03:09,890
MAN: You're renting the house for twelve months after all, aren't you?

57
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:12,360
SHELLEY: Yes. OK, well I...

58
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:16,975
MAN:... sorry to interrupt. I just thought of another furniture rental company.

59
00:03:16,975 --> 00:03:22,360
It's called Space Rentals. And it's located very near to the house.

60
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,560
SHELLEY: OK.

61
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:26,463
MAN: I don't have any information about their charges,

62
00:03:26,463 --> 00:03:31,980
so it's best to use their app to find out what it would cost you to use them.

63
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:34,910
SHELLEY: OK thanks. I'll do that.

64
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:37,100
MAN: One good thing about that company is that

65
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:40,638
if you don't like the furniture once it's delivered,

66
00:03:40,638 --> 00:03:45,220
you can request exchanges - as long as you do that within a week of receiving it.

67
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:53,150
SHELLEY: That sounds really great. OK. Well thanks very much. That's so helpful...
